# Shopping-bag commit source proposal

This is an unexecuted source proposal. Author: Codex morph_review. No project module, test, native process, guard probe or transaction has been executed by this author. Root owns actual candidate validation, artifact finalization, independent contract approval, exclusive dispatch and persisted checks.

The source installs the 34 exact prepared targets from shopping-bag-delivery-preparation-r02/execution-r01. It replaces only the two prospective metadata/document artifacts with root-finalized sources and adds only individually described, absent evidence files under docs/assets/sources/shopping-bag-delivery-review-2026-10-17/final-evidence/. The image, lexical delta and three affected test afterimages remain exact. A separate postcommit copy may preserve the actual receipt at docs/assets/sources/shopping-bag-delivery-review-2026-10-17/commit/receipt.json.

## Root contract

Use input.template.json only as a field guide; its unbound status and nulls fail validation. The actual input must be saved at build/professional-english/shopping-bag-root-commit-r01/input.json. The exclusive invocation is:

`node build/professional-english/shopping-bag-commit-proposal-r01/commit.cjs <source_SHA256> build/professional-english/shopping-bag-root-commit-r01/input.json <input_SHA256> <64_lowercase_hex_token>`

The token hash is SHA256 of the token's UTF-8 text. The contract hash is SHA256 of pretty JSON with two spaces plus a final newline, exactly as exported encode() writes it. It excludes the authorization envelope and independent-review descriptor, avoiding a circular review binding. The independent review must bind that contract, identify a nonempty reviewer other than the author or dispatcher, and state status accepted_exact_shopping_bag_commit_contract with accepted true. This is a programmatic witness of root's reviewed authorization, not an authentication system.

Source witnesses include the exact commit.cjs, the unchanged guarded-transaction.cjs helper, actual candidate runner, and four validator closure files. Every descriptor contains path, bytes and sha256. Paths are normalized repository-relative paths. The candidate directory must be a shopping-bag-projected-validation-r03-or-later directory; r01 failed and r02 remains undispatched. Runner, input, actual successful receipt, callback count and command exit witness are all explicit contract fields. The runner must retain its reviewed source hash. No candidate success is claimed by this proposal.

The protected input union starts with the frozen 5,085-file preparation binding and the r01 dependency supplement, deduplicating to 5,097, then the r02 media supplement, yielding 5,120. The actual candidate's explicitly described dependency supplements add the remaining callback closure. Each supplemental JSON has a files array of path, bytes and sha256 or raw_sha256. Additional supplement paths must be beneath the exact reviewed candidate directory. The final union must exactly equal the candidate input map; its count and sorted-map hash are bound in the contract. No hardcoded final count or earlier candidate success is accepted.

The target commitment is SHA256(encode(targetRows(buildChanges(contract, io)))). Build changes only after final sources and individual evidence additions are bound; the target commitment itself is not used to construct bytes. For root construction, calculate rows using the frozen preparation plan and exact finalized artifacts, then set the commitment before invoking buildChanges. The two finalized source descriptors must differ from the prospective preparation artifacts. Final metadata must keep actual commit/persisted fields null or false until separate immutable receipts exist; it should identify the future committed journal as the activation evidence. Root's independent review checks this documentary meaning.

## Read-only API and transaction behavior

Importing commit.cjs loads built-ins and performs no filesystem reads or writes. validate(input, io, invocation) and buildChanges(contract, io) use injected read/exists adapters and do not mutate files. Invocation contains repository_root, source_sha256 and token. realAdapter(root) is exported for root-owned wrappers; each read rejects symlinks/junctions, non-files and unsafe or escaping paths. Path guards include Windows forbidden characters, reserved names, case aliases, ancestor overlaps and transaction/evidence overlap.

run() checks the exact source and input, then validates the complete review, candidate, preimages, absent targets and input closure before consuming execution-r01. Preflight guard failures create no attempt or production changes. After preflight passes, execution-r01 is one-shot; start, intent and success/failure are exclusive new files. Never replay a consumed execution. The helper alone owns the transaction at build/professional-english/transactions/shopping-bag-image-r01. It records exact stages/backups and a chained journal. Existing lock/journal/attempt state is rejected; interrupted recovery is a separate reviewed action. The helper offers process-interruption recovery, not power-loss atomicity or simultaneous visibility of all target files.

Actual loadProfessionalContent output is hashed using SHA256(JSON.stringify(data)), preserving loader ordering, before and after commit. The 5,120-plus protected input union, exact preparation, reviews, candidate receipts and all source artifacts are rechecked. Only four existing target files may differ from their union preimages. No tests, native process or browser are dispatched by commit.cjs. Root runs the actual audit and three affected Node suites separately after success.

## Committed receipt and persisted verifier

The committed receipt contains status committed, committed true, source/input/contract bindings, independent review, source witnesses, candidate receipt and callback count, input_union (path, sha256, count, pin_map_sha256), unaffected_input_count, transaction_dir, plan_sha256, prepared_sha256, state (path and sha256), target_manifest, journal summary, exact before/after registry hashes and persisted_validation_completed false with persisted_validation_receipt null. Later checks produce a new receipt; never amend this receipt to claim a later success.

A persisted wrapper first pins this receipt and commit.cjs bytes using independent trusted hashes. Then call verifyCommittedJournal(io, receipt). This built-in-only verifier checks the prepared plan, exact stages/backups, current target afterimages, complete applying/applied state sequence, the trusted committed final-state path/hash and absence of an active lock. io additionally supplies list(directory), returning only names in that directory. A rewritten internally consistent state chain fails the final trusted hash. The verifier does not run a project module or infer persisted audit/test success.

## Outstanding acceptance

Independent source/contract review, actual successful candidate validation, finalized metadata/evidence, root guard probes, actual commit and persisted verification are still required. Existing failed candidates and historical evidence remain immutable. This source proposal is not asset integration, curriculum completion or ready-module acceptance.
